# Which cup contains starch? The Lugol colour test
#
# Compare the same dilute iodine/iodide test solution with and without ordinary
# cornstarch. In a real activity ask an adult first, protect clothes and the
# table from iodine stains, wear eye protection, and do not taste lab mixtures.
register lv1

# Control: dilute Lugol solution is brown in water. This vessel has the same
# water and indicator dose as the test vessel but no starch.
add v1 water 100mL
add v1 Lugol-Lösung_1% 2mL
inspect v1

# Test: first make an identical brown control, then change just one thing by
# adding cornstarch. Iodide keeps iodine in the aqueous inventory; sufficiently
# long starch helices contribute the computed broad absorption band, so the
# visible state becomes blue-black without consuming the starch or KI.
new beaker
add v2 water 100mL
add v2 Lugol-Lösung_1% 2mL
inspect v2
add v2 Speisestärke 1g
inspect v2

# Try flour, potato or a sugar control only after their named material recipes
# exist. Different starch sources and heating can alter the real colour; this
# lesson deliberately models the reviewed cornstarch surrogate at room
# temperature rather than treating every white powder as starch.
